      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "5236346109362176"
    },
    {
      "content": "I would send out one truck and I would send out two movers. Our hourly rate for a two man crew is $208 per hour and it takes effect once they actually get on site. The hourly rate is all inclusive. So we don't have any trip fees, there's no taxes there's no credit card fees we had and wrap all the furniture items to prevent damages we have tools on-hand so we can disassemble and reassemble things like the day bed or the crib and everything is insured. We can also disconnect and reconnect the washer and dryer as long as there's no gas lines. The only thing for that was, we need a liability waiver signed since we aren't certified plumbers but we can also handle that. And then the way that it works James, is we do a two and a half hour minimum which is $520 once we exceed the minimum we bill in fifteen minute increments until the move is completed, so you only pay for the time that is used that day. Does that all make sense?",
